{#
  The questionnaire invitation.

  ── WHY IT IS NOT THE PLAIN-TEXT NOTE IT USED TO BE ────────────────────────

  This went out through `OtpService::sendCustom`, which is `isHTML(false)`. So the one
  message on the platform that asks a nominee to do real work — write about themselves,
  gather documents, upload them — arrived looking like a system notice, next to a
  branded voting broadcast that only asked them to share a link. The ask that needs the
  most trust had the least of it.

  ── AND WHY IT REUSES final-hours.twig's SKELETON ──────────────────────────

  Every inbox-compatibility decision in the <head> and wrapper of that file was paid for
  once and is not worth re-deriving: fluid-hybrid width with an MSO conditional for
  Outlook (which ignores max-width), a hosted PNG mark rather than a data: URI (Gmail,
  Outlook and Yahoo all refuse data: in an img src), an explicit dark palette rather than
  a defensive one, `mso-line-height-rule: exactly` so Word does not collapse long
  paragraphs, and a styled preheader. Diverging from it would mean discovering the same
  things again in somebody's Outlook.

  ── WHAT IS DIFFERENT, DELIBERATELY ────────────────────────────────────────

  · No countdown GIF. A ticking clock is right for "voting closes in six hours" and
    wrong for a task that takes an evening — it says hurry to somebody who needs to go
    and find a letter from 2019. The deadline is a line of text.
  · The deadline block renders ONLY when there is one, and never claims the form locks.
    It does not: the questionnaire stays open afterwards. Saying otherwise to hurry
    somebody along would be a lie the platform then contradicts.
  · The two fraud/honesty lines from the old plain-text body are kept verbatim in
    substance. They are the most important sentences in the message — "nothing here
    costs money" is what protects a nominee from somebody impersonating us — so they are
    set as real content, not footer small print.

  ── REBUILT 3 OCT 2026: THE HANDOFF'S LADDER, AND ACCENT'S COLOURS ──────────

  Deleted and written again from docs/handoff/inventory/_emails.md (owner, 3 Oct 2026).
  Type sits on REFERENCE §6.2's closed ladder — the 10px and 11px labels are 11.5, and
  nothing is smaller but the 1px preheader collapse, which is a hiding device and not
  type (TypeScaleTest). px is right here: no Display & reading setting reaches an inbox,
  and rem is ignored by enough clients to be a gamble. Every colour is `c.<token>`,
  `Accent::mail()` passed in by the sender under the handoff's own names — mail cannot
  read `var()`, but it need not type a palette of its own either, and this file used to
  type thirty-odd colours that were in no palette at all. The dark-mode block is ink as
  the ground and ground as the words, as the newsletter's always was: the handoff names
  no dark palette, so none is invented. The mono and capitals rules are for screens
  (MonoAndCaseTest leaves mail out), so the tracked micro-labels keep their voice.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no, date=no, address=no, email=no, url=no">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>Tell the judges about your work — Africa GATES</title>
<!--[if mso]>
<noscript>
<xml>
<o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
<o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch>
</o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
</xml>
</noscript>
<![endif]-->
<style>
  body, table, td, a { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
  table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; }
  img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; border: 0; height: auto; line-height: 100%; outline: none; text-decoration: none; display: block; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; background-color: {{ c.ground }}; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse !important; }
  a[x-apple-data-detectors] { color: inherit !important; text-decoration: none !important; font-size: inherit !important; font-family: inherit !important; font-weight: inherit !important; line-height: inherit !important; }
  u + #body a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  #MessageViewBody a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  span.MsoHyperlink { color: inherit; mso-style-priority: 99; }
  [data-ogsc] .agw-bg { background-color: {{ c.surface }} !important; }
  [data-ogsc] .agw-text { color: {{ c.ink }} !important; }

  /* Outlook (Word engine) ignores line-height unless told the rule is exact, and
     collapses to single spacing on long paragraphs. */
  p, td, a, div, h1 { mso-line-height-rule: exactly; }

  /* ── DARK MODE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `color-scheme: light` above already stops Apple Mail and iOS inverting anything,
     which is why the palette below is a deliberate dark counterpart rather than a
     defensive one — Accent's ink as the ground and its ground as the words, because
     the handoff names no dark palette and this file will not invent one. Gmail's and Outlook.com's dark modes invert regardless and do it
     badly on near-white surfaces — dark text left on a darkened background. Declaring
     the dark values explicitly means the clients that DO honour the query render a
     chosen design, and the ones that force-invert have less to get wrong. */
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .agw-body   { background-color: {{ c.ink }} !important; }
    .agw-bg     { background-color: {{ c.ink }} !important; }
    .agw-text   { color: {{ c.ground }} !important; }
    .agw-muted  { color: {{ c.line }} !important; }
    .agw-body-t { color: {{ c.tint }} !important; }
    .agw-hero   { background-color: {{ c['ink-2'] }} !important; }
    .agw-rule   { border-color: {{ c['ink-2'] }} !important; }
    /* The green CTA already clears 4.5:1 against white text, so it is left alone —
       lightening it here would only reduce that. */
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
    .agw-wrapper { width: 100% !important; }
    .agw-px { padding-left: 28px !important; padding-right: 28px !important; }
    .agw-headline { font-size: 26px !important; line-height: 32px !important; }
    .agw-btn-pad { padding-left: 28px !important; padding-right: 28px !important; }
    .agw-hero-pad { padding: 28px 20px !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body id="body" class="agw-body" style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:{{ c.ground }};">

{# The brand mark is a HOSTED PNG, not an inlined data: URI.

   It was base64 — 20,848 bytes, over half the entire email — and Gmail, Outlook desktop,
   Outlook.com and Yahoo all refuse data: URIs in an img src, so the majority of readers
   paid that weight and saw the alt text anyway. It also spent half the headroom before
   Gmail's ~102KB clipping point, and what Gmail clips off a campaign is the footer, which
   is where the unsubscribe link lives.

   Not the SVG at /assets/img/logo-africa-gates.svg either: it is 1.4MB of embedded
   bitmap, and email clients do not render SVG at all. #}
<!-- PREHEADER -->
<div style="display:none; max-height:0; overflow:hidden; mso-hide:all; font-size:1px; line-height:1px; color:{{ c.ground }}; opacity:0;">
  The judges only have what somebody else wrote about you. Tell them in your own words.
  &nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;&nbsp;&zwnj;
</div>

<table role="presentation" class="agw-body" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="{{ c.ground }}" style="background-color:{{ c.ground }};">
<tr>
<td align="center" style="padding:32px 12px;">


  <!--[if mso]>
  <table role="presentation" width="560" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:560px;"><tr><td>
  <![endif]-->
  {# FLUID-HYBRID, not a fixed 560px table.

     This was width="560" with the mobile override living only inside the one @media
     block. Gmail strips <style> in several configurations (notably a non-Gmail address
     fetched via POP/IMAP into a Gmail account), and when it does, a 560px table lands on
     a 320px screen: the reader gets a horizontally scrolling email or a zoomed-out one.
     A percentage width with a max-width needs no media query to work, and the MSO
     conditional above gives Outlook — which ignores max-width — its fixed 560. #}
  <table role="presentation" class="agw-wrapper agw-bg" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:100%; max-width:560px; background-color:{{ c.surface }}; border-radius:20px; overflow:hidden;">

    <!-- DARK HEADER BAR (logo left, status badge right) -->
    <tr>
      <td style="background-color:{{ c.ink }};">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
          <tr>
            <td class="agw-px" style="padding:20px 32px;">
              <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
                <tr>
                  <td valign="middle">
                    <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                      <tr>
                        <td valign="middle" width="40" style="padding-right:10px;">
                          {# THE MARK ONLY, not the full lockup. The wordmark version is
                             illegible below about 96px, and the words "Africa GATES" are
                             already set in live text in the cell beside this one — printing
                             them twice, once as unreadable pixels, is worse than not
                             printing them at all.

                             Served at 2x (192px for a 40px box) so it is not soft on a
                             retina phone, which is where most of these are opened. #}
                          <img src="{{ site_url }}/assets/img/logo-mark.png" width="40" height="40" alt="Africa GATES" style="display:block;">
                        </td>
                        <td valign="middle">
                          <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.surface }}; line-height:16px;">Africa</p>
                          <p style="margin:1px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:2px; color:{{ c['green-light'] }}; line-height:14px;">GATES</p>
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                    </table>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="middle" align="right">
                    <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:1.6px; color:{{ c.line }}; text-transform:uppercase;">Your nomination</p>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <!-- WHAT THIS IS -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" style="padding:36px 40px 0 40px;">
        <h1 class="agw-headline agw-text" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:28px; line-height:34px; color:{{ c.ink }}; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Tell the judges<br><span style="color:{{ c.green }};">in your own words</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="agw-body-t" style="margin:14px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:23px; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }};">
          {% if first_name %}{{ first_name }}, you{% else %}You{% endif %} have been nominated for an Africa GATES award{% if programme %} &mdash; {{ programme }}{% endif %}{% if category_name %}, in {{ category_name }}{% endif %}.
        </p>
        <p class="agw-body-t" style="margin:12px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:23px; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }};">
          Right now the judges have only what the person who nominated you wrote. We would
          like to hear about the work from you, and to see anything you can show us.
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <!-- THE LINK -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px agw-btn-pad" align="center" style="padding:30px 40px 0 40px;">
        <!--[if mso]>
        <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="{{ link }}" style="height:48px;v-text-anchor:middle;width:300px;" arcsize="12%" strokecolor="{{ c.green }}" fillcolor="{{ c.green }}">
        <w:anchorlock/>
        <center style="color:{{ c.surface }};font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;">Open my questionnaire</center>
        </v:roundrect>
        <![endif]-->
        <!--[if !mso]><!-->
        <a href="{{ link }}" target="_blank" style="display:inline-block; width:100%; max-width:300px; box-sizing:border-box; background-color:{{ c.green }}; border-radius:8px; padding:15px 24px; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.surface }}; text-decoration:none; text-align:center;">
          Open my questionnaire
        </a>
        <!--<![endif]-->
        {# The URL in full, as text. This link IS the nominee's whole credential — they have
           no account — so a reader whose client mangles the button, or who wants to move it
           to a laptop, needs the address itself and not just something to click. #}
        <p class="agw-muted" style="margin:14px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:17px; color:{{ c.soft }}; word-break:break-all;">
          {{ link }}
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <!-- WHAT IT INVOLVES -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" style="padding:32px 40px 0 40px;">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
          <tr>
            <td style="border-left:2px solid {{ c.green }}; padding:2px 0 2px 16px;">
              <p class="agw-body-t" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }};">
                A short questionnaire, and room to add your own work: links, documents,
                photographs, reports, letters, press coverage &mdash; whatever exists.
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <p class="agw-muted" style="margin:16px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:21px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
          You do not have to finish it in one sitting. The page saves as you go and the
          link keeps working.
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>

    {# THE DEADLINE, only when there is one — and it never says the form closes, because it
       does not. See QuestionnairePolicy. #}
    {% if deadline %}
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" style="padding:24px 40px 0 40px;">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="{{ c.ground }}" style="background-color:{{ c.ground }}; border-radius:10px;">
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:14px 18px;">
              <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:1.2px; color:{{ c.soft }}; text-transform:uppercase;">Please send it by</p>
              <p class="agw-text" style="margin:4px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.ink }};">{{ deadline }}</p>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endif %}

    <!-- THE TWO THINGS WORTH SAYING PLAINLY -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" style="padding:30px 40px 0 40px;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:1.2px; color:{{ c.soft }}; text-transform:uppercase;">
          Two things worth saying plainly
        </p>
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
          <tr>
            <td width="30" valign="top" style="padding:1px 14px 18px 0;">
              <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.green }};">01</p>
            </td>
            <td valign="top" style="padding-bottom:18px;">
              <p class="agw-body-t" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }};">
                <strong style="color:{{ c.ink }};">Nothing here costs money.</strong> We will never
                ask you to pay for a nomination, an interview, a result or an award. If
                anybody does, it is not us.
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td width="30" valign="top" style="padding:1px 14px 0 0;">
              <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:{{ c.green }};">02</p>
            </td>
            <td valign="top">
              <p class="agw-body-t" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:{{ c['ink-2'] }};">
                <strong style="color:{{ c.ink }};">Answering honestly about what has not worked
                has never cost anybody an award.</strong> The judges are looking for real work,
                not a perfect record.
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <!-- CLOSING -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" style="padding:34px 40px 0 40px;">
        <p class="agw-muted" style="margin:0 0 2px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:{{ c.soft }};">We are glad you were nominated,</p>
        <p class="agw-text" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight:700; font-size:14px; color:{{ c.ink }};">The Africa GATES Team</p>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <!-- FOOTER -->
    <tr>
      <td class="agw-px" align="center" style="padding:36px 40px 32px 40px;">
        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
          <tr><td style="border-top:1px solid {{ c['line-3'] }}; font-size:0; line-height:0; padding-bottom:22px;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:1.2px; color:{{ c.green }}; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase;">Africa G.A.T.E.S.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
          {{ postal_address }}
        </p>
        <p style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5px; color:{{ c.soft }};">
          <a href="{{ site_url }}" style="color:{{ c.soft }}; text-decoration:underline;">africagates.org</a>{% if unsubscribe_url %}&nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:{{ c.soft }}; text-decoration:underline;">Unsubscribe</a>{% endif %}
        </p>
      </td>
    </tr>

  </table>
  <!--[if mso]>
  </td></tr></table>
  <![endif]-->

</td>
</tr>
</table>

</body>
</html>
